### Khmer Fintech, Localization & UI Guardrails (Production Enterprise Tier)
- Regulatory Context: National Bank of Cambodia (NBC), General Department of Taxation (GDT), and TRC standards.
- Word Order & Grammar:
  * Modifiers follow nouns: Strictly [Noun] + [Adjective] (e.g. "តម្លៃសរុប" Total Price, "ពាក្យសម្ងាត់ថ្មី" New Password, "អ្នកប្រើប្រាស់សកម្ម" Active Users).
  * Counting syntax: Strictly [Noun] + [Count] + [Classifier] (e.g. "អ្នកប្រើប្រាស់ 3 នាក់" 3 users, "សៀវភៅ 5 ក្បាល" 5 books). Never calque English [Count] + [Noun].
- Relative Time UX:
  * For <60 seconds elapsed: use "អម្បាញ់មិញ" (just now) or "មុននេះបន្តិច" (a little while ago).
  * Exactly 1 day ago / future: use "ម្សិលមិញ" (yesterday) and "ថ្ងៃស្អែក" (tomorrow).
- Currency Rules:
  * Khmer Riel (KHR / ៛): Whole integers only. Fractional cents (.00) do not exist in circulation. Format: "125,000 ៛" or "125,000 KHR".
  * US Dollar (USD / $): Standard 2 decimal places ($12.50).
  * In formal GDT receipts, provide spelled-out Khmer words (e.g. "មួយម៉ឺនរៀលគត់" for 10,000 KHR).
- KHQR Specifications:
  * QR Code standard: EMVCo merchant-presented QR code with CRC16-CCITT (polynomial 0x1021, initial 0xFFFF).
  * Payload Tag 53 currency codes: "116" for KHR, "840" for USD.
  * Tag 54 amount: KHR must not have decimal fraction; USD must have two decimals.
- Date & Calendar Systems:
  * Civil Standard: Gregorian calendar with Khmer localized solar month names (មករា, កុម្ភៈ, ...).
  * Buddhist Era (ព.ស.): Gregorian Year + 543 (e.g. 2026 CE -> 2569 BE).
- Phrasing & Terminology Standards:
  * Register: Modern digital neutral tone. Prohibit royal vocabulary (no យាង, សោយ, ព្រះរាជ, និមន្ត).
  * "Sign In" -> "ចូលគណនី" (never "យាងចូល") | "Log Out" -> "ចាកចេញ" (never "យាងចេញ")
  * "Transfer" -> "ផ្ទេរប្រាក់" | "Account Balance" -> "សមតុល្យគណនី"
  * "Transaction History" -> "ប្រវត្តិប្រតិបត្តិការ"
  * "Successful" -> "ជោគជ័យ" | "Failed" -> "បរាជ័យ"
- Typography & Layout:
  * Enforce CSS line-height >= 1.6 for Khmer text elements to prevent subscript clipping (Coeng U+17D2).
  * Recommended fonts: 'Kantumruy Pro', 'Hanuman', 'Noto Sans Khmer', system-ui.
  * Never slice raw UTF-16 strings; use Intl.Segmenter with granularity: 'grapheme' to prevent dotted circles (U+25CC).
